I did the math you'll need 228 consecutive passes on metal IPv6 to get it back to 95% :sweat:

That's only ~114 test runs a day to get it in for Friday Branch Cut. That means you'll need to kick a test off every ~13 minutes (just kidding, don't do that).

@Miciah @jcmoraisjr Anyways, just a heads up, you'll likely have to advocate for an exception to get this in before branch cut.

We're still below the 95% threshold on metal/ipv6. It went from 0% to 21% after we gangway'ed it with 6 runs that succeed. Before that we had a wrong assumption about the loopback address being always 127.0.0.1 on all platforms, making it to always fail on ipv6 only ones.

Also, Azure should be just below the threshold (93%) due to a [flake](https://prow.ci.openshift.org/view/gs/prow-artifact-archive/logs/periodic-ci-openshift-release-main-ci-4.22-e2e-azure-ovn-techpreview/2040608310754807808) that we analyzed and realized to be infra related. There were no further action here regarding code changes.

@everettraven we should be good on this promotion if we discard the Azure flake, and specially the first failing runs on metal/ipv6: it was fixed only in the test, no changes in the production code. Moreover, the feature gate is just enabling the user to use dynamic configuration. It defaults as disabled, so the default behavior continues the same.
